Hello R-SIG-ECOLOGY members

Geographic patterns often add essential context to environmental data analysis. Advanced QGIS: Spatial Analysis led by Nick Bearman (University College London and Geospatial Training Solutions) is now available as an on-demand streaming seminar. Apply spatial overlays, point-based access analysis, spatial joins, and aggregation to create interpretable geographic metrics in QGIS. Integrate XY coordinates, postal data, and other datasets while evaluating the capabilities and constraints of spatial analysis. Ecologists and environmental researchers can use these techniques alongside R-based workflows to examine vegetation, soils, hydrology, and spatial relationships.

Course details: https://instats.org/seminar/advanced-qgis-spatial-analysis-1
The course page includes the curriculum and enrollment details.


